  message: "FLEET GATE LANDED (PR merged 86a58ce952). The bare->method magnet gate is now wired across ALL method-dispatch analyzers: the 3 funnel langs (Scala/Swift/D, merged earlier) + 11 more via a verified multi-agent workflow (go, rust, php, js_ts, csharp, groovy, dart, lua, zig, cpp, objc). Shared defer_bare_method_call helper (analyze/base.py, generalized with a separator param for Owner::method langs). Each analyzer withholds a weak-suffix/ambiguous bind to a cross-class method, emitting unresolved + enclosing_class instead of a false high-confidence calls edge; free funcs/objects, same-class implicit this/self, and exact/import-scoped matches still resolve. 21020 tests green, 100% coverage; every wiring TDD-red-confirmed + adversarially verified. ruby (already had its own INV-fahub cascade) and nim (no cross-class magnet) correctly excluded. REMAINING for the flip: (1) Site-1 MRO walkers for the fleet langs to RECOVER inherited implicit-this/self calls (PR-2, needs per-language inheritance-edge validation); (2) D free-form nested-local residual (WI-situj); (3) the cross-language validation bakeoff."  # d70d
